      "html": "<div data-citation-items=\"%5B%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19922179%2Fitems%2FSPC5LXWA%22%5D%2C%22itemData%22%3A%7B%22id%22%3A%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19922179%2Fitems%2FSPC5LXWA%22%2C%22type%22%3A%22article%22%2C%22abstract%22%3A%22We%20introduce%20%24%CE%A8_0%24%20(Psi-Zero)%2C%20an%20open%20foundation%20model%20to%20address%20challenging%20humanoid%20loco-manipulation%20tasks.%20While%20existing%20approaches%20often%20attempt%20to%20address%20this%20fundamental%20problem%20by%20co-training%20on%20large%20and%20diverse%20human%20and%20humanoid%20data%2C%20we%20argue%20that%20this%20strategy%20is%20suboptimal%20due%20to%20the%20fundamental%20kinematic%20and%20motion%20disparities%20between%20humans%20and%20humanoid%20robots.%20Therefore%2C%20data%20efficiency%20and%20model%20performance%20remain%20unsatisfactory%20despite%20the%20considerable%20data%20volume.%20To%20address%20this%20challenge%2C%20%5C%5Cours%5C%5C%3Bdecouples%20the%20learning%20process%20to%20maximize%20the%20utility%20of%20heterogeneous%20data%20sources.%20Specifically%2C%20we%20propose%20a%20staged%20training%20paradigm%20with%20different%20learning%20objectives%3A%20First%2C%20we%20autoregressively%20pre-train%20a%20VLM%20backbone%20on%20large-scale%20egocentric%20human%20videos%20to%20acquire%20generalizable%20visual-action%20representations.%20Then%2C%20we%20post-train%20a%20flow-based%20action%20expert%20on%20high-quality%20humanoid%20robot%20data%20to%20learn%20precise%20robot%20joint%20control.%20Our%20research%20further%20identifies%20a%20critical%20yet%20often%20overlooked%20data%20recipe%3A%20in%20contrast%20to%20approaches%20that%20scale%20with%20noisy%20Internet%20clips%20or%20heterogeneous%20cross-embodiment%20robot%20datasets%2C%20we%20demonstrate%20that%20pre-training%20on%20high-quality%20egocentric%20human%20manipulation%20data%20followed%20by%20post-training%20on%20domain-specific%20real-world%20humanoid%20trajectories%20yields%20superior%20performance.%20Extensive%20real-world%20experiments%20demonstrate%20that%20%5C%5Cours%5C%5C%20achieves%20the%20best%20performance%20using%20only%20about%20800%20hours%20of%20human%20video%20data%20and%2030%20hours%20of%20real-world%20robot%20data%2C%20outperforming%20baselines%20pre-trained%20on%20more%20than%2010%24%5C%5Ctimes%24%20as%20much%20data%20by%20over%2040%5C%5C%25%20in%20overall%20success%20rate%20across%20multiple%20tasks.%20We%20will%20open-source%20the%20entire%20ecosystem%20to%20the%20community%2C%20including%20a%20data%20processing%20and%20training%20pipeline%2C%20a%20humanoid%20foundation%20model%2C%20and%20a%20real-time%20action%20inference%20engine.%22%2C%22DOI%22%3A%2210.48550%2FARXIV.2603.12263%22%2C%22language%22%3A%22en%22%2C%22license%22%3A%22Creative%20Commons%20Attribution%20Non%20Commercial%20Share%20Alike%204.0%20International%22%2C%22note%22%3A%22version%3A%201%22%2C%22publisher%22%3A%22arXiv%22%2C%22source%22%3A%22DOI.org%20(Datacite)%22%2C%22title%22%3A%22%24%CE%A8_0%24%3A%20An%20Open%20Foundation%20Model%20Towards%20Universal%20Humanoid%20Loco-Manipulation%22%2C%22title-short%22%3A%22%24%CE%A8_0%24%22%2C%22URL%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Farxiv.org%2Fabs%2F2603.12263%22%2C%22author%22%3A%5B%7B%22family%22%3A%22Wei%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Songlin%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Jing%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Hongyi%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Li%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Boqian%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Zhao%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Zhenyu%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Mao%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Jiageng%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Ni%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Zhenhao%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22He%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Sicheng%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Liu%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Jie%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Liu%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Xiawei%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Kang%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Kaidi%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Zang%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Sheng%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Yuan%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Weiduo%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Pavone%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Marco%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Huang%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Di%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Wang%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Yue%22%7D%5D%2C%22accessed%22%3A%7B%22date-parts%22%3A%5B%5B%222026%22%2C7%2C2%5D%5D%7D%2C%22issued%22%3A%7B%22date-parts%22%3A%5B%5B%222026%22%5D%5D%7D%7D%7D%5D\" data-schema-version=\"9\"><p>Psi-Zero : Loco-motion Tasks, Decoupling learning process by staging training paradigm with different learning objectives, Dexterous manipulation</p>\n<p>Pretrained VLM backbone on large-scale egocentric human videos</p>\n<p>Posttrained flow-based action expert on high-quality humanoid robot data</p>\n<p></p>\n<p>Human-robot unified action space</p>\n<p>MM-DiT for action sequence in joint space</p>\n<p></p>\n<p>LangWBC, LeVERB</p>\n<p>Dexterous Manipulation: Being-H0</p>\n<p></p>\n<p></p>\n<p><img alt=\"\" width=\"1409\" height=\"489\" data-attachment-key=\"ZXE58TZZ\"></p>\n<p>Psi-0:</p>\n<p>1.Architecture - Triple-system</p>\n<p>System 2: Qwen3-VL-2B</p>\n<p>↓ VLM Features</p>\n<p>System 1: MM-DiT - 8DoF</p>\n<p><img alt=\"\" width=\"546\" height=\"396\" data-attachment-key=\"6Z7VEFJA\"></p>\n<p>System 0: AMO</p>\n<p></p>\n<p>Training Recipe</p>\n<p> 1) Ego-centric Human Video: EgoDex</p>\n<p><span class=\"highlight\" data-annotation=\"%7B%22attachmentURI%22%3A%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19922179%2Fitems%2FSB3KNU2W%22%2C%22pageLabel%22%3A%223%22%2C%22position%22%3A%7B%22pageIndex%22%3A3%2C%22rects%22%3A%5B%5B263.5235162000002%2C293.7660784000003%2C300.0165200000002%2C302.40365260000027%5D%2C%5B48.959%2C281.8110784000003%2C300.01651999999996%2C290.4486526000003%5D%2C%5B48.959%2C269.85607840000034%2C300.01652%2C278.4936526000003%5D%2C%5B48.959%2C257.20508280000035%2C300.0180542%2C268.4311054000003%5D%2C%5B48.95900000000006%2C245.2500828000003%2C300.01595421999997%2C254.93234360000034%5D%2C%5B48.95900000000003%2C233.65135000000035%2C300.01382659999996%2C244.52110540000035%5D%2C%5B48.95900000000003%2C221.69635000000034%2C277.30421899999993%2C232.56610540000034%5D%5D%7D%2C%22citationItem%22%3A%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19922179%2Fitems%2FSPC5LXWA%22%5D%2C%22locator%22%3A%223%22%7D%7D\">“We use a shared action representation for both human hands and robot end-effectors. Specifically, the 48-DoF action in task space is defined as a ≜ {al, ar} and each al or ar ∈ R24 is {Twrist, Pthumb, Pindex, Pmiddle, Pring, Ppinky}. The T ∈ R9 is the 9-DoF wrist pose vector consisting of 3D position and 6D rotation. Each P ∈ R3 is a 3D fingertip position.”</span> <span class=\"citation\" data-citation=\"%7B%22citationItems%22%3A%5B%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19922179%2Fitems%2FSPC5LXWA%22%5D%2C%22locator%22%3A%223%22%7D%5D%2C%22properties%22%3A%7B%7D%7D\">(<span class=\"citation-item\">Wei 等, 2026, p. 3</span>)</span></p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\" data-indent=\"1\">Tokenize - FAST</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\" data-indent=\"1\"><img alt=\"\" width=\"434\" height=\"78\" data-attachment-key=\"ETSZ2B5N\"></p>\n<p>2) Post-Training - action expert- Cross-task Real Humanoid Data</p>\n<p><img alt=\"\" width=\"391\" height=\"53\" data-attachment-key=\"KB2PKYP4\"></p>\n<p>3) Fine-Tuning on In-Domain Data - Few-shots</p>\n<p><img alt=\"\" width=\"1075\" height=\"605\" data-attachment-key=\"LW5GJNLD\"></p>\n<p></p>\n<p></p>\n<p>Real time Chunking</p>\n<p>Kevin Black, Allen Z Ren, Michael Equi, and Sergey Levine. Training-time action conditioning for efficient real-time chunking. arXiv preprint arXiv:2512.05964, 2025.</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\" data-indent=\"1\">d = uniform(0, dmax)</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\" data-indent=\"1\">dmax ∈ [0, H − s)</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\" data-indent=\"1\"></p>\n<p>Tailoring Teleopration for Loco-Manipulation</p>\n<p>Separate upper-body pose tracking, dexterous manipulation and locomotion commands</p>\n<p>PICO + Wrist Trackers - Upper-body</p>\n<p>Waist + Foot Trackers - Lower-body</p>\n<p></p>\n<p></p>\n</div>",
